6.2 EpsRange :𝜀-sampling in Higher
Dimensions
Now, we present the generalization of the Eps2D algorithm to higher
dimensions ( 𝑑≥2), referred to as the EpsRange algorithm. The
preprocessing phase remains unchanged: we compute an 𝜀-sample
N𝜀of the datasetD, of size𝑚, for a chosen parameter 𝜀. We know
that𝑚≪𝑛, because the VC-dim of stripe ranges is 𝛿=𝑑+1[50].
During query time, the algorithm proceeds similarly to Eps2D .
In Step i, we find the 𝑖ℓ-th and𝑖𝑢-th points inN𝜀according to the
scoring function 𝑓. In Step ii, we solve a high-dimensional instance
of the SRRproblem. The resulting set D𝑜contains candidate points
fromDthat lie between the scores of the 𝑖ℓ-th and𝑖𝑢-th ranked
points in the sample. This set is a conformal set for the relaxed
problem|D𝑜|-RAR . To obtain the exact solution, we proceed to
Step iii, where we perform a high-dimensional range counting
query to determine the exact rank of each point in D𝑜. Finally, in
Step iv, we sort the candidates in D𝑜and return the point with
exact rank𝑖, completing the solution to the RAR selection problem.
Analysis . The analysis is similar to the 2D case, provided in Ap-
pendix I. The results are as follows:
