7 Experiments
In this section, we evaluate the performance of our algorithms in
both the random-access ranked retrieval and similarity search set-
tings. Our implementation is available at this anonymous repository .
We begin by describing the datasets. Next, we present results for
thestripe range searching subtask showcasing our proposed hierar-
chical index (Subsection 7.1). We then evaluate our methods on two
primary tasks: random-access ranked retrieval (Subsection 7.2) and
random-access similarity search (Subsection 7.3). Additional results
and experimental details are deferred to Appendix M.
Datasets . For the ranked retrieval, we use synthetic and real-world
datasets. The synthetic dataset is generated from a Zipfian distri-
bution. Our real-world datasets include US Used Cars [75] (3M
records, 66 columns), FIFA 2023 [63] (300K records, 54 columns),
andUS Flights [94] (5M records, 31 columns). For the similarity
search setting, we evaluate our methods on five popular benchmark
datasets from ann-benchmarks.com :SIFT-128-Euclidean [58] (1M
vectors,ℓ2),Fashion-MNIST-784-Euclidean [99] (60K vectors, ℓ2),
GIST-960-Euclidean [58] (1M vectors, ℓ2),GloVe-100-Angular [80]
(1M vectors, cosine), and GloVe-25-Angular [80] (1M vectors, co-
sine).13More details of the datasets are provided in Appendix M.1.
7.1 Stripe Range Retrieval
For the SRRproblem, we compare against classical and widely used
range searching indices, including KD-Tree [ 16], R-Tree [ 49], and
Partition Tree [ 71], and Ball Trees [ 77]. Our proposed hierarchical
index is abbreviated as Hierarchical . As a baseline, we also include
a simple linear search approach, denoted as Exhaustive . To apply
the baseline range searching indices to stripe range queries, we
traverse the tree top-down, pruning subtrees whose corresponding
hyperrectangles do not intersect the query stripe (see Algorithm 4).
More experiments on SRR problem is provided in Appendix M.2.
7.1.1 Synthetic Dataset. We begin by evaluating the performance
of the algorithms on synthetic datasets.
