8 Conclusion
We studied the problem of Random-Access Ranked Retrieval ( RAR)
and Random-Access Similarity Search ( RAS). We showed that RAS
can be reduced to RAR . For solving the general RAR problem, we
first proposed an algorithm based on geometric arrangements with
logarithmic query time but an exponential space complexity. Next,
we proposed our space-efficient algorithms based on 𝜀-samples. By
providing a hierarchical sampling-based data structure for efficient
stripe-range retrieval, we developed a practical algorithm for the
relaxed𝜅-RAR problem that scales to hundreds of dimensions.
